WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.760
The first extended trailer for Pixar's Cars
3 just dropped and it teases some intriguing

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.490
things for the second sequel in the Cars franchise.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.809
In this video I'm going to take a look some
points you might have missed in the extended

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:16.500
look trailer as well as some easter eggs which
might impact the Pixar Theory for Cars.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.400
The trailer starts with the same scenes from
the teaser which see Lightning McQueen end

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.100
up in a serious crash that sends him spinning
through the air.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.580
The new trailer also shows the crash from
some different angles and with some crucial

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.580
differences.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.300
As the trailer begins, you'll notice it's
actually daytime and if you look carefully

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.340
you can't really see any fully animated faces
in the spectator vehicles that are looking

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.340
on.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.260
The colours are muted, everything has been
dulled down and you don't see any faces in

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.710
the on-looking RVs.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:48.070
There's also a heartbeat and breathing sound
overlaid on top of the action, and all of

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.720
these things point to the fact that something
beyond the obvious going on here.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.230
OK, let's jump forward to later in the trailer
where we see the crash from another angle.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:01.850
The crash happens at the Los Angeles International
Speedway in both of the scenes, but here it's

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.390
actually night time with the racetrack lit
by the stadium lights.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:10.950
Also the onlooking spectators and RVs are
properly animated with proper Cars faces and

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:11.950
eyes.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:12.950
So why the difference?

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:17.310
Well, it seems likely that the first crash
scene that happens during the day with a dulled

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.760
and grey background is actually a dream sequence
or flashback that Lightning experiences later

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.760
in the movie.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.850
We know that after the crash, Lightning has
to retrain with Cruz Ramirez to find how he's

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.350
going to get his form back.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.000
So, this could be a nightmare that Lightning
suffers during his recovery process.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.520
There are also some nice teases to what we
might expect from Lightning's recovery, including

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.350
a couple of new looks and paint jobs.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:43.659
During his crash, Lightning is still sporting
more or less the same look from Cars 1 and

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:47.040
the beginning of Cars 2 with his classic Rust-eze
logo on the back.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.780
But in a later scene where he visits an old
disused speedway track with Cruz Ramirez,

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.750
we can see he's had a new paint job.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:58.439
He's now got a sort of souped up, much larger
Rust-eze logo on his side and another on his

00:01:58.439 --> 00:01:59.439
back end.

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:03.420
He also has Lightning McQueen emblazoned in
bright fluorescent letters just above his

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.630
side windows.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:08.750
And later in a pit-stop scene, the Rust-eze
logo has changed again, reducing back down

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.140
in size but still different to the style from
the first two movies.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.290
Jackson Storm is clearly the new champion
on the block, and we can see him collecting

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:20.810
an award, presumably the Piston Cup, and all
the while Lightning is looking on from the

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.810
corner.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.650
His number looks like 20 but the design has
inserted a small point between the two and

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:30.310
the zero, which feel like a subtle reference
to the fact that Storm represents the upcoming

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.970
new generation of race cars, so he's a kind
of version 2.0.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:39.040
And also, the symbol on the side of Jackson
Storm is appropriately based on the international

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.230
hurricane symbol.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:43.610
It's been tweaked and stretched and colour
matched with his other blue colours to give

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.840
him a sleek look.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.450
The trailer also flashes through some of the
tech that is powering the new upstart racer.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:53.450
These screens show he can change his tyre
pressure according to track conditions and

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:58.020
which race track he on, and he's also perfected
his skills and speed with access to a racing

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.020
simulator.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.959
There's a neat Buy n Large easter egg which
you can spot as a track sponsor at one of

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:03.959
the speedways.

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:08.739
And this could be further clue that ties the
Cars franchise into Jon Negroni's Pixar Theory.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:12.459
Remember BnL is the corporation in WALL�E
that basically enabled the pollution of the

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:15.970
planet and sent humans away from Earth while
it attempted to clear it up.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:20.240
The Pixar Theory suggests that Cars takes
place after humans leave the planet and before

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.880
a time hundreds of years later when the events
of WALL�E take place.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:28.020
The presence of Buy n Large as a corporate
sponsor in Cars 3 shows the corporation is

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.550
still very much active on Earth at this time.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:35.459
There are some other new sponsors teased in
the trailer including the Grandol Oil company

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:40.720
and Frostar Air Filters, while Dinoco is clearly
still the sponsor of the Piston Cup series.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.550
And there's a new Thunder Hollow Speedway
where there seems to be some pretty full-on

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.580
Mad Max style racing going on.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.989
So far, neither Lightning's trusty pal Mater
nor his girlfriend Sally have appeared in

00:03:50.989 --> 00:03:55.569
any trailers, but the characters are confirmed
to appear in Cars 3 and were included in footage

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:57.600
shown at the Detroit Auto Show.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.980
So guys what did you think of the extended
look trailer?

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:03.730
Were there any other easter eggs you spotted
and what do you think about the look of Lightning's

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.120
new rival Jackson Storm?

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.519
I'd love to hear your thought in the comments
below!

